[h1]Phobos Banking[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.3.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - held draft, awaiting owner gameplay checks

Debt follows a spacer everywhere. Ogiso's Bank holds the mortgage you started with, the broker holds the one on your ship, and the station office books its fines the same way. Phobos Banking puts all of it on your wrist, and finds you a lender when you need one.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A CREDIT app[/b] on the PDA home screen. Tap it and the PDA closes and the Credit panel opens, as the game's own Roster and Duties apps do.
[*][b]Loans and mortgages[/b]: each one's lender, balance, next instalment, how many instalments are left and when it was taken out, worked out exactly as the game charges them.
[*][b]Bills to pay[/b]: instalments, docking fees and late fees waiting in your ledger, late ones first, with the late fee the next shift change will add if a bill stays unpaid.
[*][b]Regular charges[/b], such as crew wages, and how often each falls due.
[*][b]An overview[/b]: cash on hand, the total left to repay, the next instalments and the bills waiting.
[*][b]Open Finances[/b] takes you to the game's own Finances window, where bills are paid.
[*][b]Lenders[/b]: who lends where, at what rate, and what they would lend you now, or the one thing in the way.
[*][b]Borrow[/b] from a lender where you are: the money is paid in, and the loan is a mortgage in your ledger, repaid by the shift. The lender's interest is billed on what you still owe at each shift change. You see the first instalment and the whole loan's interest before you confirm.
[*][b]Finance a ship or an apartment[/b]: get a pre-approval, then buy at the broker with as little as 30% to 40% down instead of 50%. The mortgage becomes the lender's, and selling the ship repays them first.
[*]Three accredited lenders: Corvane Mutual at OKLG, Halcyon Bond on Mars for those the Xinhua administration likes, Aerie Savings Union on Venus.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosbank debts, lenders, borrow, loans, approve and withdraw.
[/list]

[h2]Shape the market yourself[/h2]
Lenders are a data file. Add your own, or change who lends where, to whom and at what rate, in BepInEx/config/PhobosBank/lenders, or ship them in an add-on. A lender can ask for standing with a faction or anything else a story can. Story writers get flags for loans taken, repaid and late.

[h2]How the game's debts work[/h2]
[list]
[*]Each shift a loan sends its instalment to your ledger as a bill.
[*]A bill still unpaid at a shift change gains a late fee of 17.5% of it, and the fee is a bill too.
[*]Selling a mortgaged ship repays the lender from the sale first.
[*]A lender's interest is a bill like any other, with the same late fee.
[*]The debts list reads your ledger; only Borrow adds to it.
[/list]

[h2]Coming later[/h2]
Unregistered lenders and their stories are planned; they are not in this version.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.127.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Banking and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Loans you take are kept in one small record on your character. Remove the mod and the app goes; the loans stay in your ledger as ordinary mortgages, with no more interest.
[*]Not paying has only the game's own consequences: late fees. Nothing is repossessed.
[*]The quick bar under the PDA's home screen is your own list in the game's settings; the app is on the home screen.
[*]Automated checks pass; in-game checks are still pending.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games or Kitfox Games. It reads the game's own ledger and opens its own Finances window. LOGUSS's Common Sense Cargo Manifest showed how a mod can add a PDA app; Phobos Framework does it independently.

The CREDIT icon is drawn by the project script. The cover scene is an original promotional illustration generated with OpenAI's image API, then composed with the project's shared frame and pixel lettering. It is not a gameplay screenshot.

